{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Read the approved RTL against its own header comment and found three distinct defects, one per failing test. Each defect has its own repro testbench, written to check only the behaviour that defect breaks. VeriTriage run-0001 classified the combined set as unknown_failure with 30% confidence, so these buckets rest on reading the RTL and are leads until the platform's simulator.run gate confirms each repro fails.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "triage_report", "title": "pwm_gen nightly triage: three failures, three buckets", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-e946df186d]. VeriTriage session [run:run-0001] covered pulse_width_fail.log, period_fail.log and duty_update_fail.log in one call. It returned unknown_failure (30% confidence, 3 evidence nodes) with 'Likely RTL bug' as the top hypothesis. That combined call cannot separate the classes, so the buckets below come from reading [artifact:prj-f58c6d66a9.design-under-investigation.a1] against its header contract. Bucket PERIOD (period_fail.log): the counter wraps at 'cnt == PERIOD - 2', so a period lasts PERIOD-1 cycles (7 instead of 8). Signature: rise-to-rise interval is 7 where 8 is expected. Repro: tb/repro_period.v. Bucket PULSE_WIDTH (pulse_width_fail.log): 'pwm <= (cnt <= duty_now)' uses <= where < belongs, so the output is high for duty+1 cycles, and duty 0 still gives a one-cycle pulse. Signature: high width is duty+1. Repro: tb/repro_pulse_width.v. Bucket DUTY_UPDATE (duty_update_fail.log): duty_q is sampled at cnt==0 but never used. The compare reads the live 'duty_now = duty', so a change in the middle of a period takes effect at once instead of in the next period. Signature: a mid-period duty increase makes pwm rise again within the same period. Repro: tb/repro_duty_update.v. Each repro is designed to pass on a correct design and when only the other two defects are present, so no repro stands for two buckets. Open items: no per-log VeriTriage runs and no same-seed reruns are in the evidence. The mapping of logs to buckets is inferred from the log names and the RTL. The repros have not yet been simulated."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/repro_period.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: PWM period length", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the PERIOD bucket of [requirement:req-e946df186d] against [artifact:prj-f58c6d66a9.design-under-investigation.a1]. Holds duty at 3, waits for the output to settle, then checks four rise-to-rise intervals equal PERIOD=8. Expected to fail on the 'cnt == PERIOD - 2' wrap, which gives 7. Prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once.", "entry": "tb"}, {"path": "tb/repro_pulse_width.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: PWM high-pulse width", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the PULSE_WIDTH bucket of [requirement:req-e946df186d] against [artifact:prj-f58c6d66a9.design-under-investigation.a1]. With constant duty 3 and then 5, it settles and checks that each high pulse lasts exactly duty cycles. Expected to fail on 'cnt <= duty_now', which gives duty+1. Prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once.", "entry": "tb"}, {"path": "tb/repro_duty_update.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: mid-period duty change deferred to next period", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the DUTY_UPDATE bucket of [requirement:req-e946df186d] against [artifact:prj-f58c6d66a9.design-under-investigation.a1]. With duty 2, it raises duty to 6 just after pwm falls. It then checks two things: pwm stays low for the rest of that period (at least 4 cycles), and the next pulse uses the new duty (5 to 7 cycles). Expected to fail because the compare reads the live 'duty' rather than duty_q. Prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once.", "entry": "tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001"], "claims": ["The three defects were identified by reading the RTL source, not by simulation.", "The mapping of period_fail.log, pulse_width_fail.log and duty_update_fail.log to the three buckets is inferred from the log names and the RTL. The log contents were not available to me.", "I expect each repro to fail on the buggy RTL and to pass on a correct pwm_gen or when only one of the other defects is present. This has not been run."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Recommended follow-ups:\n- Run veritriage.investigate on each log on its own; run-0001 was a single combined call.\n- Rerun each failure with the same seed before closing the buckets.\n\nAll three testbenches use top module 'tb', so the platform's top, taken from the first file's entry, is valid for every per-file run.\n\nThe repro gate (simulator.run with expect=fail) is run by the platform; I have not run it."}

=== FILE: tb/repro_period.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Repro for bucket PERIOD: the output must repeat every PERIOD clock cycles.
module tb;
    reg        clk = 1'b0;
    reg        rst = 1'b1;
    reg  [3:0] duty = 4'd0;
    wire       pwm;
    integer    passed = 0;
    integer    failed = 0;
    integer    cyc = 0;
    integer    t_prev, t_now, i;
    reg        done = 1'b0;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    pwm_gen #(.PERIOD(8)) dut (.clk(clk), .rst(rst), .duty(duty), .pwm(pwm));

    always #5 clk = ~clk;
    always @(posedge clk) cyc <= cyc + 1;

    task chk_eq(input [8*32-1:0] label, input integer got, input integer exp);
        begin
            if (got == exp) passed = passed + 1;
            else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $display("FAIL [%0s] got %0d expected %0d", label, got, exp);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task finish_tb;
        begin
            if (!done) begin
                done = 1'b1;
                $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
                $finish;
            end
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        #100000;
        $display("FAIL [WATCHDOG] pwm stopped toggling");
        failed = failed + 1;
        finish_tb;
    end

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
        duty = 4'd3;
        rst  = 1'b1;
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        @(negedge clk) rst = 1'b0;
        repeat (30) @(posedge clk);
        @(posedge pwm); #1 t_prev = cyc;
        for (i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
            @(posedge pwm); #1 t_now = cyc;
            chk_eq("PERIOD_RISE_TO_RISE", t_now - t_prev, 8);
            t_prev = t_now;
        end
        finish_tb;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===

