e new duty (check label DUTY_NEXT_PERIOD_APPLIED). The target cause is the live 'duty_now' comparison in place of 'duty_q' in [artifact:prj-f58c6d66a9.design-under-investigation.a1]. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the run nonce before $finish.", "entry": "tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0005"], "claims": ["By hand analysis, each repro should fail on pwm_gen_buggy.v and pass on an RTL with the three identified defects corrected; this has not been simulated by this seat.", "By hand analysis, each repro is insensitive to the other two buckets' defects taken one at a time.", "period_fail.log, pulse_width_fail.log and duty_update_fail.log correspond to buckets PERIOD, PULSE_WIDTH and DUTY_UPDATE respectively; this mapping is inferred from the log names and the RTL, not from the log contents.", "No per-log VeriTriage session and no same-seed rerun of each failure has been performed; flakiness is not ruled out by evidence."], "escalation": null, "notes": "This is a resubmission after attempt 1 was refused for naming run:run-0001, which was never recorded. The only run cited now is run:run-0005, the recorded veritriage.investigate session. The testbench content is unchanged from attempt 1, because the refusal concerned only the fabricated run reference. VeriTriage's 30% unknown_failure classification over the combined logs is not used as a bucket. Running veritriage.investigate on each log separately is recommended, in case a single log shows a class the combined input hides. All three testbenches use top module 'tb'."}

